# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQD addon v0.12 or later (`pip install qiskit-addon-sqd`)\n"
msgstr "Addon SQD v0.12 atau lebih baharu (`pip install qiskit-addon-sqd`)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "NumPy, SciPy, and Matplotlib (`pip install numpy scipy matplotlib`)\n"
msgstr "NumPy, SciPy, dan Matplotlib (`pip install numpy scipy matplotlib`)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You also need an IBM Quantum&reg; account with credentials saved locally, and access to a QPU\n"
"with at least 40 qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda juga perlukan akaun IBM Quantum&reg; dengan kelayakan yang disimpan secara setempat, dan akses kepada QPU\n"
"dengan sekurang-kurangnya 40 qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No simulator package is needed, and no data files have to be downloaded. The two interaction files\n"
"this tutorial uses are embedded in the following setup cell and written to a temporary directory when you\n"
"run it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tiada pakej simulator diperlukan, dan tiada fail data perlu dimuat turun. Dua fail interaksi\n"
"yang digunakan tutorial ini dibenamkan dalam sel persediaan berikut dan ditulis ke direktori sementara apabila anda\n"
"menjalankannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Persediaan {#setup}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section imports the tools and defines the shell-model helpers the workflow needs, in the order\n"
"the workflow uses them. The physics behind each one is derived in the [Appendix](#appendix); the\n"
"comments describe each function’s role in the workflow.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bahagian ini mengimport alat dan mentakrifkan pembantu model petala yang diperlukan aliran kerja, mengikut susunan\n"
"yang digunakan aliran kerja. Fizik di sebalik setiap satu diterbitkan dalam [Lampiran](#appendix); komen\n"
"menerangkan peranan setiap fungsi dalam aliran kerja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two interaction files are unpacked first. Both are published parameter sets, embedded here so the\n"
"notebook is self-contained: `usda.snt` is the USDA $sd$-shell Hamiltonian [\\[2\\]](#references) and\n"
"`gxpf1.snt` is the GXPF1 $pf$-shell Hamiltonian [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dua fail interaksi dinyahmampat dahulu. Kedua-duanya ialah set parameter yang diterbitkan, dibenamkan di sini supaya\n"
"notebook ini berdikari: `usda.snt` ialah Hamiltonian petala-$sd$ USDA [\\[2\\]](#references) dan\n"
"`gxpf1.snt` ialah Hamiltonian petala-$pf$ GXPF1 [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The model space and the qubit register {#the-model-space-and-the-qubit-register}"
msgstr "Ruang model dan daftar qubit {#the-model-space-and-the-qubit-register}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An `.snt` file holds the model space, the single-particle energies, and the $J$-coupled two-body\n"
"matrix elements. For the mass-dependent interactions used here, the third and fourth fields of the two-body\n"
"header specify the reference mass\n"
"$A_{\\mathrm{ref}}$ at which the interaction was fitted and the exponent of its mass dependence. Both\n"
"files carry the exponent $-0.3$, with $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ for USDA and $42$ for GXPF1, so the\n"
"tabulated matrix elements must be rescaled by $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{-0.3}$ for the nucleus being\n"
"computed [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references). Single-particle energies are not rescaled. Skipping\n"
"this step changes the correlation energy by a few percent.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fail `.snt` menyimpan ruang model, tenaga zarah tunggal, dan unsur matriks dua-jasad\n"
"berganding-$J$. Bagi interaksi bergantung-jisim yang digunakan di sini, medan ketiga dan keempat pengepala\n"
"dua-jasad menentukan jisim rujukan\n"
"$A_{\\mathrm{ref}}$ di mana interaksi itu dipadankan dan eksponen kebergantungan jisimnya. Kedua-dua\n"
"fail membawa eksponen $-0.3$, dengan $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ untuk USDA dan $42$ untuk GXPF1, jadi\n"
"unsur matriks yang dijadualkan mesti diskalakan semula dengan $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{-0.3}$ untuk nukleus yang\n"
"dikira [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references). Tenaga zarah tunggal tidak diskalakan semula. Melangkau\n"
"langkah ini mengubah tenaga korelasi sebanyak beberapa peratus.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The energies that follow are *valence* energies, measured from the inert core; they are not experimental\n"
"separation energies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tenaga yang menyusul ialah tenaga *valens*, diukur dari teras lengai; ia bukan tenaga\n"
"pemisahan eksperimen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clebsch-Gordan recoupling {#clebsch-gordan-recoupling}"
msgstr "Penggandingan semula Clebsch-Gordan {#clebsch-gordan-recoupling}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Equation (2) requires Clebsch-Gordan coefficients for half-integer angular momenta. Every argument is\n"
"passed as *twice* its physical value, so $j = 5/2$ enters as `5` and the arithmetic stays exact.\n"
msgstr ""
"Persamaan (2) memerlukan pekali Clebsch-Gordan untuk momentum sudut separuh-integer. Setiap hujah\n"
"diberikan sebagai *dua kali ganda* nilai fizikalnya, jadi $j = 5/2$ dimasukkan sebagai `5` dan aritmetik kekal tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`Interaction.v_ms` handles lookups of the interaction matrix elements. An `.snt` file stores each\n"
"matrix element once, so a lookup might need the antisymmetrized pair-exchange phase $-(-1)^{j_a + j_b - J}$ on either\n"
"side, and the bra and ket might be stored in either order.\n"
msgstr ""
"`Interaction.v_ms` mengendalikan carian unsur matriks interaksi. Fail `.snt` menyimpan setiap unsur\n"
"matriks sekali sahaja, jadi satu carian mungkin memerlukan fasa pertukaran-pasangan tak-simetri $-(-1)^{j_a + j_b - J}$ pada mana-mana\n"
"sisi, dan bra serta ket mungkin disimpan dalam mana-mana susunan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Matrix elements and the symmetry test {#matrix-elements-and-the-symmetry-test}"
msgstr "Unsur matriks dan ujian simetri {#matrix-elements-and-the-symmetry-test}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A determinant is a sorted tuple of occupied qubit indices. Two determinants differing in more than\n"
"two occupied states have a vanishing matrix element; otherwise, the Slater-Condon rules give a short\n"
"sum over the interaction, multiplied by a fermionic sign counting how many occupied states lie between the\n"
"operators in the fixed register ordering.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penentu ialah tupel tersusun bagi indeks qubit yang diduduki. Dua penentu yang berbeza dalam lebih daripada\n"
"dua keadaan diduduki mempunyai unsur matriks lenyap; jika tidak, petua Slater-Condon memberikan hasil tambah\n"
"pendek ke atas interaksi, didarab dengan tanda fermion yang mengira berapa banyak keadaan diduduki terletak di antara\n"
"pengendali dalam susunan daftar tetap.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`symmetry_allowed` is the integer test that all four exact quantum numbers reduce to. It is used both\n"
"to filter samples and to enumerate the exact basis for the runs small enough to check.\n"
msgstr ""
"`symmetry_allowed` ialah ujian integer yang diturunkan daripada keempat-empat nombor kuantum tepat. Ia digunakan untuk\n"
"menapis sampel dan juga untuk menyenaraikan asas tepat bagi larian yang cukup kecil untuk disemak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reference determinant {#the-reference-determinant}"
msgstr "Penentu rujukan {#the-reference-determinant}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ansatz is built on top of a single determinant, so that determinant should be the best one\n"
"available. Filling the lowest single-particle energies ignores the two-body interaction. In these model\n"
"spaces, that choice gives an energy 1–2 MeV above the lowest-energy determinant.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ansatz dibina di atas satu penentu, jadi penentu itu hendaklah yang terbaik\n"
"yang ada. Mengisi tenaga zarah tunggal terendah mengabaikan interaksi dua-jasad. Dalam ruang model\n"
"ini, pilihan itu memberikan tenaga 1–2 MeV di atas penentu bertenaga terendah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Restricting to fillings made of time-reversed $(+m_j, -m_j)$ pairs forces $M_J = 0$ exactly and\n"
"leaves only $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ candidates per species (a few thousand at most), so the\n"
"best one can be found by searching them all on the full diagonal $\\langle \\Phi | H | \\Phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Ties go to the most strongly aligned pairs, where the $J = 0$ pairing force is strongest. In every\n"
"case in this tutorial that can be checked against a full enumeration, the search returns the global\n"
"lowest-diagonal determinant, which is also the largest single component of the exact ground state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menghadkan kepada pengisian yang terdiri daripada pasangan songsang-masa $(+m_j, -m_j)$ memaksa $M_J = 0$ dengan tepat dan\n"
"hanya meninggalkan $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ calon bagi setiap spesies (paling banyak beberapa ribu), jadi\n"
"yang terbaik boleh dicari dengan menyelidik kesemuanya pada pepenjuru penuh $\\langle \\Phi | H | \\Phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Seri diberikan kepada pasangan yang paling kuat sejajar, di mana daya pemasangan $J = 0$ paling kuat. Dalam setiap\n"
"kes dalam tutorial ini yang boleh disemak dengan penyenaraian penuh, carian memulangkan penentu\n"
"berpepenjuru terendah global, yang juga merupakan komponen tunggal terbesar bagi keadaan dasar tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The excitation pool and its perturbative ranking {#the-excitation-pool-and-its-perturbative-ranking}"
msgstr "Kolam pengujaan dan kedudukan perturbatifnya {#the-excitation-pool-and-its-perturbative-ranking}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Correlation is carried by two-particle–two-hole ($2p2h$) excitations from the reference. Two\n"
"selection rules reduce the pool before any circuit is built: an excitation must conserve $M_J$, and the hole pair and particle\n"
"pair must be able to couple to a common total $J$, which is a triangle inequality.\n"
msgstr ""
"Korelasi dibawa oleh pengujaan dua-zarah–dua-lohong ($2p2h$) daripada rujukan. Dua\n"
"petua pemilihan mengurangkan kolam sebelum sebarang litar dibina: pengujaan mesti mengekalkan $M_J$, dan pasangan lohong serta pasangan\n"
"zarah mesti boleh bergandingan kepada $J$ jumlah yang sama, iaitu ketaksamaan segi tiga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The remaining excitations are ranked by the Epstein-Nesbet second-order score of selected configuration interaction\n"
"[\\[4\\]](#references),\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengujaan yang tinggal disusun mengikut skor peringkat kedua Epstein-Nesbet bagi interaksi konfigurasi terpilih\n"
"[\\[4\\]](#references),\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"s_\\alpha = \\frac{|\\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle|^2}{|\\Delta_\\alpha|},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\Delta_\\alpha = H_{\\mathrm{ref},\\mathrm{ref}} - H_{\\alpha\\alpha},\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"s_\\alpha = \\frac{|\\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle|^2}{|\\Delta_\\alpha|},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\Delta_\\alpha = H_{\\mathrm{ref},\\mathrm{ref}} - H_{\\alpha\\alpha},\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which estimates how much correlation energy each excitation carries. The same two numbers fix the\n"
"circuit angle: with $V = \\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle$, the first-order amplitude\n"
"is $t_\\alpha = V / \\Delta_\\alpha$. The [Appendix](#appendix) explains why the first-order amplitude is\n"
"the choice used in this tutorial rather than the exact two-level angle.\n"
msgstr ""
"yang menganggarkan berapa banyak tenaga korelasi yang dibawa setiap pengujaan. Dua nombor yang sama menetapkan\n"
"sudut litar: dengan $V = \\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle$, amplitud peringkat pertama\n"
"ialah $t_\\alpha = V / \\Delta_\\alpha$. [Lampiran](#appendix) menerangkan mengapa amplitud peringkat pertama ialah\n"
"pilihan yang digunakan dalam tutorial ini dan bukannya sudut dua-aras yang tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qubit-excitation blocks {#qubit-excitation-blocks}"
msgstr "Blok pengujaan qubit {#qubit-excitation-blocks}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Under the Jordan-Wigner mapping a particle-conserving $2p2h$ excitation operator becomes a sum of\n"
"eight Pauli strings, each carrying a string of $Z$ operators between the outermost indices. The\n"
"$Z$ strings enforce fermionic antisymmetry, and they are expensive: a proton-neutron\n"
"excitation spans the boundary between the two halves of the register and includes a parity string\n"
"across that boundary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di bawah pemetaan Jordan-Wigner, pengendali pengujaan $2p2h$ pemeliharaan-zarah menjadi hasil tambah\n"
"lapan rentetan Pauli, setiap satu membawa rentetan pengendali $Z$ antara indeks paling luar. Rentetan\n"
"$Z$ menguatkuasakan ketaksimetrian fermion, dan ia mahal: pengujaan proton-neutron\n"
"merentangi sempadan antara dua separuh daftar dan merangkumi rentetan kepariti\n"
"merentasi sempadan itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dropping the $Z$ strings gives the *qubit-excitation* operator of Yordanov et al.\n"
"[\\[5\\]](#references). The state prepared by this operator has different amplitudes, but it connects exactly the same pairs of determinants, so the set of determinants the circuit can\n"
"reach is unchanged. Pooled SQD uses these determinants for the classical diagonalization. Step 2 compares\n"
"the support of the two constructions and measures their hardware costs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggugurkan rentetan $Z$ memberikan pengendali *pengujaan-qubit* Yordanov et al.\n"
"[\\[5\\]](#references). Keadaan yang disediakan oleh pengendali ini mempunyai amplitud yang berbeza, tetapi ia menghubungkan pasangan penentu yang sama, jadi set penentu yang boleh dicapai litar\n"
"tidak berubah. SQD terkumpul menggunakan penentu ini untuk pepenjuruan klasik. Langkah 2 membandingkan\n"
"sokongan kedua-dua pembinaan dan mengukur kos perkakasannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Building the Pauli form from $a_j^\\dagger = \\tfrac{1}{2}(X_j - i Y_j) \\otimes Z_{<j}$, with the $Z$\n"
"string optional, keeps the two constructions a single flag apart. All eight terms of one generator\n"
"commute, so a single `PauliEvolutionGate` step is the exact exponential rather than a Trotter\n"
"approximation to it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Membina bentuk Pauli daripada $a_j^\\dagger = \\tfrac{1}{2}(X_j - i Y_j) \\otimes Z_{<j}$, dengan rentetan $Z$\n"
"bersifat pilihan, mengekalkan kedua-dua pembinaan hanya berbeza satu bendera. Kesemua lapan sebutan satu penjana\n"
"berkomut, jadi satu langkah `PauliEvolutionGate` ialah eksponen tepat dan bukannya\n"
"penghampiran Trotter kepadanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The depth budget and the circuit ensemble {#the-depth-budget-and-the-circuit-ensemble}"
msgstr "Bajet kedalaman dan ensembel litar {#the-depth-budget-and-the-circuit-ensemble}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A single deep circuit containing every ranked excitation can exceed the hardware’s coherence time. Spreading the pool\n"
"over an *ensemble* of shallow circuits and pooling their shots into one determinant set turns Step 2\n"
"into a packing problem: each excitation has a measured cost, each circuit has a budget, and the\n"
"question is how much of the ranked pool fits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu litar dalam tunggal yang mengandungi setiap pengujaan tersusun boleh melebihi masa koheren perkakasan. Menyebarkan kolam\n"
"ke atas *ensembel* litar cetek dan mengumpulkan shot-nya ke dalam satu set penentu menjadikan Langkah 2\n"
"satu masalah pembungkusan: setiap pengujaan mempunyai kos terukur, setiap litar mempunyai bajet, dan\n"
"soalannya ialah berapa banyak kolam tersusun yang muat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The budget is measured in **two-qubit depth** (layers of two-qubit gates on the critical path)\n"
"rather than in a raw gate count, because depth sets the circuit's duration and therefore how\n"
"much of the device's coherence it spends. The total count is reported alongside it, since that is the\n"
"better proxy for accumulated gate error; the two answer different questions and neither substitutes\n"
"for the other.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bajet diukur dalam **kedalaman dua-qubit** (lapisan gate dua-qubit pada laluan kritikal)\n"
"bukannya bilangan gate mentah, kerana kedalaman menetapkan tempoh litar dan oleh itu berapa banyak\n"
"koheren peranti yang digunakan. Jumlah bilangan dilaporkan bersama-samanya, kerana itulah\n"
"proksi yang lebih baik bagi ralat gate terkumpul; keduanya menjawab soalan berbeza dan tiada satu pun menggantikan\n"
"yang satu lagi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both quantities are extracted by *arity*: an instruction acting on exactly two qubits, whatever the\n"
"backend happens to call its entangling gate. Matching on gate names instead could return zero\n"
"for an unfamiliar basis set, incorrectly placing the whole pool in one circuit without exceeding\n"
"the computed budget.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua-dua kuantiti diekstrak mengikut *arity*: arahan yang bertindak pada tepat dua qubit, apa pun nama yang\n"
"diberikan backend kepada gate berbelitnya. Memadankan nama gate sebaliknya boleh memulangkan sifar\n"
"bagi set asas yang tidak dikenali, lalu tersilap meletakkan seluruh kolam dalam satu litar tanpa melebihi\n"
"bajet yang dikira.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Filling whichever circuit is currently emptiest, in rank order, keeps every circuit near the budget.\n"
"Costs are measured on the real backend target, one excitation at a time, because a cost read off an\n"
"abstract circuit is not the cost the transpiler produces.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengisi litar yang paling kosong pada masa itu, mengikut susunan kedudukan, mengekalkan setiap litar hampir bajet.\n"
"Kos diukur pada sasaran backend sebenar, satu pengujaan pada satu masa, kerana kos yang dibaca daripada\n"
"litar abstrak bukanlah kos yang dihasilkan oleh transpiler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-processing: repair, recombine, diagonalize {#post-processing-repair-recombine-diagonalize}"
msgstr "Pasca-pemprosesan: baiki, gabung semula, pepenjuru {#post-processing-repair-recombine-diagonalize}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three helpers do the work of Step 4.\n"
msgstr "Tiga pembantu melakukan kerja Langkah 4.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`half_configurations` splits each sampled row into a proton half and a neutron half, and keeps each\n"
"half that has the correct nucleon number. A row with a valid proton half contributes that half even if its\n"
"neutron half has the wrong nucleon number. Each half carries the total sampled weight of the rows it appeared in, which\n"
"is what ranks it if the subspace needs to be truncated.\n"
msgstr ""
"`half_configurations` memisahkan setiap baris yang disampel kepada separuh proton dan separuh neutron, dan mengekalkan setiap\n"
"separuh yang mempunyai bilangan nukleon yang betul. Baris dengan separuh proton yang sah menyumbang separuh itu walaupun\n"
"separuh neutronnya mempunyai bilangan nukleon yang salah. Setiap separuh membawa jumlah berat sampel baris tempat ia muncul, yang\n"
"menentukan kedudukannya jika subruang perlu dipotong.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`grow_subspace` recombines the halves into every product that lands in the target $M_J$ and parity\n"
"sector, *adding* to the subspace it is given rather than rebuilding it. That keeps successive\n"
"subspaces nested, which is what makes the energy sequence monotone non-increasing instead of merely\n"
"fluctuating around a bound.\n"
msgstr ""
"`grow_subspace` menggabungkan semula separuh-separuh itu menjadi setiap hasil darab yang jatuh dalam sektor $M_J$ dan kepariti\n"
"sasaran, dengan *menambah* kepada subruang yang diberikan dan bukannya membinanya semula. Itu mengekalkan subruang\n"
"berturutan bersarang, dan itulah yang menjadikan jujukan tenaga tidak menokok secara monoton dan bukannya sekadar\n"
"berubah-ubah di sekitar satu batas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`recovery_loop` is the self-consistent configuration recovery of the pooled SQD paper\n"
"[\\[1\\]](#references): repair the two half-register nucleon numbers against the current occupancy\n"
"estimate, recombine, diagonalize, and take the next occupancy estimate from the eigenvector.\n"
msgstr ""
"`recovery_loop` ialah pemulihan konfigurasi konsisten-diri dalam kertas SQD terkumpul\n"
"[\\[1\\]](#references): baiki dua bilangan nukleon separuh-daftar berdasarkan anggaran okupansi\n"
"semasa, gabung semula, pepenjuru, dan ambil anggaran okupansi seterusnya daripada vektor eigen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Check the bit-ordering conventions carefully to avoid incorrect results. `qiskit-addon-sqd` writes column 0 of its\n"
"bitstring matrix as the *highest* qubit index, so reversing a row gives occupation indexed by qubit;\n"
"its \"right\" half is the low qubit indices, which is the proton block. Correspondingly,\n"
"`recover_configurations` takes `num_elec_a` as the proton number and average occupancies ordered\n"
"`(protons, neutrons)` by qubit index. The addon assumes bit $i$ pairs with bit $i + N$; in this\n"
"register, proton qubit $i$ and neutron qubit $i + N$ are the same $(n, \\ell, j, m_j)$ state, so the\n"
"assumption is physically meaningful here rather than incidental.\n"
msgstr ""
"Semak konvensyen susunan bit dengan teliti untuk mengelakkan keputusan yang salah. `qiskit-addon-sqd` menulis lajur 0 matriks\n"
"rentetan bitnya sebagai indeks qubit *tertinggi*, jadi membalikkan satu baris memberikan okupansi yang diindeks mengikut qubit;\n"
"separuh \"kanan\"-nya ialah indeks qubit rendah, iaitu blok proton. Sejajar dengan itu,\n"
"`recover_configurations` mengambil `num_elec_a` sebagai bilangan proton dan okupansi purata disusun\n"
"`(protons, neutrons)` mengikut indeks qubit. Addon itu mengandaikan bit $i$ berpasangan dengan bit $i + N$; dalam\n"
"daftar ini, qubit proton $i$ dan qubit neutron $i + N$ ialah keadaan $(n, \\ell, j, m_j)$ yang sama, jadi\n"
"andaian itu bermakna secara fizikal di sini dan bukannya kebetulan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Backend, budget, and run parameters {#backend-budget-and-run-parameters}"
msgstr "Backend, bajet, dan parameter larian {#backend-budget-and-run-parameters}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every run that follows uses the same backend, the same pass managers, and the same depth budget, so the three\n"
"are directly comparable. The budget ties them together: every circuit in every\n"
"ensemble has to fit inside it, and it decides how much of a pool can be sampled at all.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap larian yang menyusul menggunakan backend yang sama, pengurus pas yang sama, dan bajet kedalaman yang sama, jadi ketiga-\n"
"tiganya boleh dibandingkan secara langsung. Bajet itu mengikat kesemuanya: setiap litar dalam setiap\n"
"ensembel mesti muat di dalamnya, dan ia menentukan berapa banyak kolam yang boleh disampel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The values here were chosen by measuring transpiled cost against a Heron target. At a two-qubit depth of 300 and 16 circuits, both 24-qubit and 40-qubit ensembles come out well under 100 microseconds per\n"
"circuit, against coherence times of a few hundred microseconds. Increasing the budget includes more of the pool but increases circuit duration. Measure this\n"
"tradeoff for your backend.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nilai di sini dipilih dengan mengukur kos yang ditranspile terhadap sasaran Heron. Pada kedalaman dua-qubit 300 dan 16 litar, kedua-dua ensembel 24-qubit dan 40-qubit adalah jauh di bawah 100 mikrosaat bagi setiap\n"
"litar, berbanding masa koheren beberapa ratus mikrosaat. Menaikkan bajet memasukkan lebih banyak kolam tetapi menambah tempoh litar. Ukur\n"
"langkah timbal balik ini untuk backend anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale hardware example {#small-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Contoh perkakasan skala kecil {#small-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section follows the four-step workflow on a QPU, using the same backend and the same\n"
"gate budget as the large-scale runs. The smaller problem provides an exact reference for checking the result.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bahagian ini mengikuti aliran kerja empat langkah pada QPU, menggunakan backend yang sama dan bajet\n"
"gate yang sama seperti larian skala besar. Masalah yang lebih kecil menyediakan rujukan tepat untuk menyemak hasilnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The small-scale problem is $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$: two valence protons and two valence neutrons in the\n"
"$sd$ shell above an $^{16}\\mathrm{O}$ core, with the USDA interaction [\\[2\\]](#references). Three\n"
"orbitals per species give 24 qubits, and the complete symmetry-allowed basis is 640 determinants,\n"
"small enough to compare the energy estimates with the exact answer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah skala kecil ialah $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$: dua proton valens dan dua neutron valens dalam petala\n"
"$sd$ di atas teras $^{16}\\mathrm{O}$, dengan interaksi USDA [\\[2\\]](#references). Tiga\n"
"orbital bagi setiap spesies memberikan 24 qubit, dan asas lengkap dibenarkan simetri ialah 640 penentu,\n"
"cukup kecil untuk membandingkan anggaran tenaga dengan jawapan tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik kepada masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Read the interaction, build the register, and construct the reference determinant. The following table shows the register information from the [Background](#background), read directly\n"
"from the interaction file.\n"
msgstr ""
"Baca interaksi, bina daftar, dan bina penentu rujukan. Jadual berikut menunjukkan maklumat daftar daripada [Latar belakang](#background), dibaca terus\n"
"daripada fail interaksi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run two checks on the Hamiltonian before continuing. Both are inexpensive and can reveal\n"
"recoupling errors that a single energy calculation might not detect.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jalankan dua semakan pada Hamiltonian sebelum meneruskan. Kedua-duanya murah dan boleh mendedahkan\n"
"ralat penggandingan semula yang mungkin tidak dikesan oleh satu pengiraan tenaga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A rotationally invariant Hamiltonian organizes its eigenstates into $J$ multiplets, so every\n"
"eigenvalue of the $M_J = 2$ sector must also appear in the $M_J = 0$ spectrum at the same energy. The gap between the ground state and the lowest state carrying $M_J = 2$ is the $2^+$ excitation\n"
"energy, which is measured: $1.634$ MeV for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ [\\[6\\]](#references). An empirical\n"
"$sd$-shell interaction is expected to agree within a few hundred keV.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hamiltonian tak-berubah-putaran menyusun keadaan eigennya ke dalam multiplet $J$, jadi setiap\n"
"nilai eigen sektor $M_J = 2$ mesti juga muncul dalam spektrum $M_J = 0$ pada tenaga yang sama. Jurang antara keadaan dasar dan keadaan terendah yang membawa $M_J = 2$ ialah tenaga\n"
"pengujaan $2^+$, yang telah diukur: $1.634$ MeV untuk $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ [\\[6\\]](#references). Interaksi\n"
"petala-$sd$ empirikal dijangka setuju dalam lingkungan beberapa ratus keV.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, construct the operator pool. Applying the two selection rules gives an important result: for this reference, in this model space, **there are no allowed single excitations at all**.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, bina kolam pengendali. Menggunakan dua petua pemilihan memberikan keputusan penting: untuk rujukan ini, dalam ruang model ini, **tiada pengujaan tunggal yang dibenarkan langsung**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The reason is specific and checkable. A $1p1h$ excitation conserves $M_J$ only if the particle state\n"
"has the same $m_j$ as the hole. The reference occupies the two states of largest $|m_j|$ in the\n"
"lowest orbital ($m_j = \\pm 5/2$ of $0d_{5/2}$), and no other orbital in the $sd$ shell reaches\n"
"$|m_j| = 5/2$, since $0d_{3/2}$ stops at $3/2$ and $1s_{1/2}$ at $1/2$. Therefore, no single excitation\n"
"survives, and correlation is carried entirely by $2p2h$ excitations. This is a property of the\n"
"reference and the shell, not a general law; the following cell counts it rather than assuming it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebabnya khusus dan boleh disemak. Pengujaan $1p1h$ mengekalkan $M_J$ hanya jika keadaan zarah\n"
"mempunyai $m_j$ yang sama dengan lohong. Rujukan menduduki dua keadaan $|m_j|$ terbesar dalam\n"
"orbital terendah ($m_j = \\pm 5/2$ bagi $0d_{5/2}$), dan tiada orbital lain dalam petala $sd$ mencapai\n"
"$|m_j| = 5/2$, kerana $0d_{3/2}$ berhenti pada $3/2$ dan $1s_{1/2}$ pada $1/2$. Maka, tiada pengujaan tunggal\n"
"yang bertahan, dan korelasi dibawa sepenuhnya oleh pengujaan $2p2h$. Ini ialah sifat\n"
"rujukan dan petala, bukan hukum am; sel berikut mengiranya dan bukannya mengandaikannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Transpilation reveals the hardware cost of the Jordan-Wigner $Z$ strings and the savings from\n"
"using qubit excitations. The first cell measures both constructions against the real backend\n"
"target and checks the claim, introduced in the [Setup](#setup), that dropping the $Z$ strings changes the\n"
"amplitudes but not the set of determinants the circuit can reach.\n"
msgstr ""
"Transpilasi mendedahkan kos perkakasan rentetan $Z$ Jordan-Wigner dan penjimatan daripada\n"
"menggunakan pengujaan qubit. Sel pertama mengukur kedua-dua pembinaan terhadap sasaran backend\n"
"sebenar dan menyemak dakwaan, yang diperkenalkan dalam [Persediaan](#setup), bahawa menggugurkan rentetan $Z$ mengubah\n"
"amplitud tetapi bukan set penentu yang boleh dicapai litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compare two consequences of this substitution. A qubit excitation costs the same regardless of the distance between its\n"
"indices, so proton-neutron excitations, which span the boundary between the two halves of the\n"
"register and make up most of the pool, no longer have this additional cost. The whole pool then\n"
"fits inside the budget, which means the limit on the result is sampling rather than circuit depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bandingkan dua akibat penggantian ini. Pengujaan qubit berkos sama tanpa mengira jarak antara\n"
"indeksnya, jadi pengujaan proton-neutron, yang merentangi sempadan antara dua separuh\n"
"daftar dan membentuk sebahagian besar kolam, tidak lagi mempunyai kos tambahan ini. Seluruh kolam\n"
"kemudian muat dalam bajet, yang bermaksud had pada hasilnya ialah pensampelan dan bukannya kedalaman litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Laksanakan menggunakan primitif Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Submit one job per problem, with the whole ensemble as a single list of circuits. Gate and\n"
"measurement twirling and dynamical decoupling are enabled to reduce the effects of hardware noise.\n"
"Their benefit depends on the circuit and backend.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hantar satu job bagi setiap masalah, dengan seluruh ensembel sebagai satu senarai litar. Twirling gate\n"
"dan pengukuran serta penyahgandingan dinamik didayakan untuk mengurangkan kesan hingar perkakasan.\n"
"Manfaatnya bergantung pada litar dan backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each job’s ID is printed. Use `service.job(\"JOB_ID\")` to retrieve the completed job and its\n"
"results without using additional QPU time.\n"
msgstr ""
"ID setiap job dicetak. Gunakan `service.job(\"JOB_ID\")` untuk mendapatkan semula job yang selesai dan\n"
"keputusannya tanpa menggunakan masa QPU tambahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses dan pulangkan hasil dalam format klasik yang dikehendaki {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Convert the quantum samples into an energy estimate using the nuclear-symmetry constraints\n"
"described in the [Background](#background) section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tukarkan sampel kuantum kepada anggaran tenaga menggunakan kekangan simetri nuklear\n"
"yang diterangkan dalam bahagian [Latar belakang](#background).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Configuration recovery repairs the two nucleon numbers.** `recover_configurations` takes each shot that\n"
"has the wrong number of protons or neutrons and flips the bits least consistent with the current\n"
"estimate of the average orbital occupancies, instead of discarding it. On the first pass the\n"
"occupancy estimate comes from the shots that already survived; afterward it comes from the\n"
"eigenvector of the previous subspace, which makes the procedure self-consistent.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pemulihan konfigurasi membaiki dua bilangan nukleon.** `recover_configurations` mengambil setiap shot yang\n"
"mempunyai bilangan proton atau neutron yang salah dan membalikkan bit yang paling tidak konsisten dengan anggaran\n"
"semasa bagi purata okupansi orbital, dan bukannya membuangnya. Pada laluan pertama,\n"
"anggaran okupansi datang daripada shot yang sudah terselamat; selepas itu ia datang daripada\n"
"vektor eigen subruang sebelumnya, yang menjadikan prosedur ini konsisten-diri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**$M_J$ and parity are imposed on the recombined products, not on whole shots.** Every repaired shot\n"
"contributes a proton half and a neutron half, and the subspace is spanned by every product of a\n"
"sampled proton configuration with a sampled neutron configuration that lands at $M_J = 0$ with the\n"
"right parity. Filtering whole shots on total $M_J$ instead would throw away two good halves for the\n"
"sake of a quantum number that belongs to their combination.\n"
msgstr ""
"**$M_J$ dan kepariti dikenakan pada hasil darab yang digabung semula, bukan pada keseluruhan shot.** Setiap shot yang dibaiki\n"
"menyumbang satu separuh proton dan satu separuh neutron, dan subruang dijana oleh setiap hasil darab\n"
"konfigurasi proton yang disampel dengan konfigurasi neutron yang disampel yang jatuh pada $M_J = 0$ dengan\n"
"kepariti yang betul. Menapis keseluruhan shot pada $M_J$ jumlah sebaliknya akan membuang dua separuh yang baik demi\n"
"nombor kuantum yang dimiliki oleh gabungannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The four quantum-number checks reject different fractions of samples. The two nucleon numbers\n"
"account for most of the filtering. Parity is *automatically* satisfied inside a single major shell: every $sd$ orbital\n"
"has even $\\ell$ and every $pf$ orbital odd $\\ell$, so once the nucleon numbers are right the parity\n"
"cannot be wrong. The parity check is retained because a cross-shell model space would make it an\n"
"independent constraint. The $M_J$ check keeps products in the target angular-momentum sector. The value of\n"
"having four exact quantum numbers is that they are *cheap and exact*, not that each one is a large\n"
"filter.\n"
msgstr ""
"Empat semakan nombor kuantum menolak pecahan sampel yang berbeza. Dua bilangan nukleon\n"
"menyumbang sebahagian besar penapisan. Kepariti dipenuhi *secara automatik* dalam satu petala utama: setiap orbital $sd$\n"
"mempunyai $\\ell$ genap dan setiap orbital $pf$ $\\ell$ ganjil, jadi apabila bilangan nukleon betul, kepariti\n"
"tidak mungkin salah. Semakan kepariti dikekalkan kerana ruang model silang-petala akan menjadikannya\n"
"kekangan bebas. Semakan $M_J$ mengekalkan hasil darab dalam sektor momentum sudut sasaran. Nilai\n"
"mempunyai empat nombor kuantum tepat ialah ia *murah dan tepat*, bukan kerana setiap satu ialah penapis yang besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Diagonalizing gives a variational upper bound.** Because each iteration's subspace contains the\n"
"last, the sequence of energies falls monotonically, and every entry in it is a rigorous upper bound on\n"
"the true ground-state energy, regardless of the noise in the samples that produced it.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pepenjuruan memberikan batas atas variasi.** Memandangkan subruang setiap lelaran mengandungi yang\n"
"terdahulu, jujukan tenaga jatuh secara monoton, dan setiap entri di dalamnya ialah batas atas yang tegar bagi\n"
"tenaga keadaan dasar sebenar, tanpa mengira hingar dalam sampel yang menghasilkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate the results {#evaluate-the-results}"
msgstr "Nilaikan keputusan {#evaluate-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the following checks to evaluate your results on a Heron-class backend with these settings:\n"
msgstr "Gunakan semakan berikut untuk menilai keputusan anda pada backend kelas Heron dengan tetapan ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Shot survival** on the two nucleon numbers measures the fraction of shots with the correct proton and neutron counts. It can fall as\n"
"the register grows. A survival rate near zero can indicate a problem with circuit execution. Check the ISA depth in Step 2 and the backend's calibration, not the post-processing.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kemandirian shot** pada dua bilangan nukleon mengukur pecahan shot dengan bilangan proton dan neutron yang betul. Ia boleh jatuh apabila\n"
"daftar membesar. Kadar kemandirian hampir sifar boleh menandakan masalah dengan pelaksanaan litar. Semak kedalaman ISA dalam Langkah 2 dan kalibrasi backend, bukan pasca-pemprosesan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The recovery loop** should print a subspace dimension that stays constant or grows and an energy that stays constant or falls with\n"
"each iteration. If iteration 1 already reaches `MAX_DIMENSION`, the classical solver rather than the\n"
"sampling is the binding constraint.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Gelung pemulihan** hendaklah mencetak dimensi subruang yang kekal malar atau membesar dan tenaga yang kekal malar atau jatuh pada\n"
"setiap lelaran. Jika lelaran 1 sudah mencapai `MAX_DIMENSION`, penyelesai klasik dan bukannya\n"
"pensampelan ialah kekangan pengikat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The recovered fraction** for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ should be high, because the ansatz ceiling\n"
"computed in Step 1 is the full 640-determinant space; this run is where sampling, not\n"
"expressiveness, is the only obstacle.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pecahan yang dipulihkan** untuk $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ sepatutnya tinggi, kerana siling ansatz\n"
"yang dikira dalam Langkah 1 ialah ruang penuh 640 penentu; larian ini ialah tempat pensampelan, bukan\n"
"keekspresifan, merupakan satu-satunya halangan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The two assertions** in the preceding cell check the variational bounds. A bound that rises means the\n"
"subspaces stopped being nested, and a bound below the exact energy means something is wrong with the\n"
"Hamiltonian, not with the hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Dua penegasan** dalam sel sebelumnya menyemak batas variasi. Batas yang naik bermaksud\n"
"subruang tidak lagi bersarang, dan batas di bawah tenaga tepat bermaksud ada yang tidak kena dengan\n"
"Hamiltonian, bukan dengan perkakasan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Counterintuitively, a *noisier* backend can give a slightly better bound than a clean one, because\n"
"errors produce valid half-configurations the ideal circuit would never have sampled, and widening\n"
"a variational subspace cannot raise its lowest eigenvalue. Noisy simulation can demonstrate the same effect; this tutorial shows it with\n"
"hardware samples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara berlawanan intuisi, backend yang *lebih bising* boleh memberikan batas yang sedikit lebih baik daripada yang bersih, kerana\n"
"ralat menghasilkan separuh-konfigurasi sah yang tidak akan pernah disampel oleh litar unggul, dan melebarkan\n"
"subruang variasi tidak boleh menaikkan nilai eigen terendahnya. Simulasi berhingar boleh menunjukkan kesan yang sama; tutorial ini menunjukkannya dengan\n"
"sampel perkakasan.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/nuclear-sqd-pooled/extracted-outputs/c040-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/nuclear-sqd-pooled/extracted-outputs/c040-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Contoh perkakasan skala besar {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Scaling up changes only the inputs, so the next step is to combine the four stages into one function\n"
"and run it twice, both times on a 40-qubit register in the $pf$ shell above a\n"
"$^{40}\\mathrm{Ca}$ core with the GXPF1 interaction [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"Penskalaan hanya mengubah input, jadi langkah seterusnya ialah menggabungkan empat peringkat ke dalam satu fungsi\n"
"dan menjalankannya dua kali, kedua-duanya pada daftar 40-qubit dalam petala $pf$ di atas teras\n"
"$^{40}\\mathrm{Ca}$ dengan interaksi GXPF1 [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two runs illustrate different aspects of scaling:\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua larian menggambarkan aspek penskalaan yang berbeza:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$, two valence protons and two valence neutrons, has a 4,000-determinant basis. The\n"
"register is 40 qubits, but the problem is still small enough to diagonalize exactly on a laptop, so\n"
"you can compare the hardware result with an exact reference after increasing the register size.\n"
msgstr ""
"$^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$, dua proton valens dan dua neutron valens, mempunyai asas 4,000 penentu. Daftar\n"
"ialah 40 qubit, tetapi masalahnya masih cukup kecil untuk dipepenjurukan dengan tepat pada komputer riba, jadi\n"
"anda boleh membandingkan hasil perkakasan dengan rujukan tepat selepas menaikkan saiz daftar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$, four valence protons and four valence neutrons, has 1,963,461 symmetry-allowed determinants in the same 40 qubits.\n"
"The tutorial's dense solver cannot diagonalize that full space, so the run returns\n"
"a rigorous upper bound and the reference determinant it improves on.\n"
msgstr ""
"$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$, empat proton valens dan empat neutron valens, mempunyai 1,963,461 penentu dibenarkan simetri dalam 40 qubit yang sama.\n"
"Penyelesai tumpat tutorial ini tidak boleh memepenjurukan ruang penuh itu, jadi larian ini memulangkan\n"
"batas atas yang tegar dan penentu rujukan yang diperbaikinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Watch two quantities across the two runs. The fraction of the pool that fits inside the fixed gate\n"
"budget shrinks as the pool grows, and `pack_ensemble` reports how much is included. The\n"
"subspace stops being limited by sampling and starts being limited by `MAX_DIMENSION`, the largest\n"
"matrix the dense classical solver here builds. At this scale, a production\n"
"calculation would use a selected configuration interaction (selected-CI) solver.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan dua kuantiti merentasi dua larian. Pecahan kolam yang muat dalam bajet gate\n"
"tetap mengecil apabila kolam membesar, dan `pack_ensemble` melaporkan berapa banyak yang dimasukkan. Subruang\n"
"berhenti dihadkan oleh pensampelan dan mula dihadkan oleh `MAX_DIMENSION`, matriks\n"
"terbesar yang dibina oleh penyelesai klasik tumpat di sini. Pada skala ini, pengiraan\n"
"pengeluaran akan menggunakan penyelesai interaksi konfigurasi terpilih (selected-CI).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
