msgid "The following function calls the same stages as the walkthrough, in the same order.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi berikut memanggil peringkat yang sama seperti panduan langkah demi langkah, mengikut susunan yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "$^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$: the same workflow on a 40-qubit register {#44mathrmti-the-same-workflow-on-a-40-qubit-register}"
msgstr "$^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$: aliran kerja yang sama pada daftar 40-qubit {#44mathrmti-the-same-workflow-on-a-40-qubit-register}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The $pf$ shell above $^{40}\\mathrm{Ca}$ has four orbitals per species and 20 magnetic substates each,\n"
"so the register is 40 qubits. Two valence protons and two valence neutrons make $^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$,\n"
"with 4,000 symmetry-allowed determinants &mdash; about six times the $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ basis, using\n"
"40 qubits instead of 24.\n"
msgstr ""
"Petala $pf$ di atas $^{40}\\mathrm{Ca}$ mempunyai empat orbital bagi setiap spesies dan 20 substat magnet setiap satu,\n"
"jadi daftarnya ialah 40 qubit. Dua proton valens dan dua neutron valens membentuk $^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$,\n"
"dengan 4,000 penentu dibenarkan simetri &mdash; kira-kira enam kali ganda asas $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$, menggunakan\n"
"40 qubit dan bukannya 24.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the larger of the two examples that the notebook can solve exactly, so you can compare\n"
"the hardware result with an exact reference.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini ialah contoh yang lebih besar daripada dua contoh yang boleh diselesaikan dengan tepat oleh notebook, jadi anda boleh membandingkan\n"
"hasil perkakasan dengan rujukan tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$: beyond the tutorial's exact-diagonalization capacity {#48mathrmcr-beyond-the-tutorials-exact-diagonalization-capacity}"
msgstr "$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$: melangkaui kapasiti pepenjuruan tepat tutorial {#48mathrmcr-beyond-the-tutorials-exact-diagonalization-capacity}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Adding two protons and two neutrons uses the same 40-qubit register (`4, 4` for\n"
"$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$) and increases the basis size by a factor of about 491, to 1,963,461 symmetry-allowed determinants. That\n"
"matrix is far beyond anything this tutorial will build, so `exact=False`: there is no exact reference energy,\n"
"only the variational bound and the reference determinant it improves on.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menambah dua proton dan dua neutron menggunakan daftar 40-qubit yang sama (`4, 4` untuk\n"
"$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$) dan menaikkan saiz asas sebanyak faktor kira-kira 491, kepada 1,963,461 penentu dibenarkan simetri. Matriks\n"
"itu jauh melangkaui apa-apa yang akan dibina tutorial ini, jadi `exact=False`: tiada tenaga rujukan tepat,\n"
"hanya batas variasi dan penentu rujukan yang diperbaikinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two things change at this scale, and both are visible in the printout. The pool grows to several\n"
"hundred allowed excitations, so the fixed gate budget now covers a minority of it rather than all of\n"
"it. Also, the product subspace the samples span is larger than `MAX_DIMENSION`, so the dense solver\n"
"truncates it by sampled weight. The bound remains rigorous but can be less accurate than a bound\n"
"computed from all the sampled configurations. A production calculation would retain the samples\n"
"and use a solver that supports a larger subspace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dua perkara berubah pada skala ini, dan kedua-duanya kelihatan dalam cetakan output. Kolam itu membesar kepada beberapa\n"
"ratus pengujaan yang dibenarkan, jadi bajet gate tetap kini hanya meliputi sebahagian kecil daripadanya, bukan\n"
"keseluruhannya. Selain itu, subruang hasil darab yang dirangkumi oleh sampel lebih besar daripada `MAX_DIMENSION`, jadi pemecah padat\n"
"memotongnya mengikut berat sampel. Sempadan itu kekal tegar tetapi mungkin kurang tepat berbanding sempadan yang\n"
"dikira daripada semua konfigurasi yang disampel. Pengiraan pengeluaran akan mengekalkan sampel\n"
"dan menggunakan pemecah yang menyokong subruang yang lebih besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate a result without an exact reference {#evaluate-a-result-without-an-exact-reference}"
msgstr "Menilai hasil tanpa rujukan tepat {#evaluate-a-result-without-an-exact-reference}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$ run has no exact reference within this tutorial. Use the existing samples\n"
"to assess convergence and compare with the classical selection baseline, without additional QPU\n"
"time or full-space diagonalization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Larian $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$ tiada rujukan tepat dalam tutorial ini. Gunakan sampel sedia ada\n"
"untuk menilai penumpuan dan membandingkan dengan garis asas pemilihan klasik, tanpa masa QPU\n"
"tambahan atau pepenjuruan ruang penuh.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Is it converged?** Reorder the retained determinants by their weight in the converged eigenvector\n"
"and the subspaces become *nested*, so diagonalizing the leading $d \\times d$ block for a ladder of $d$\n"
"traces the bound's descent across two decades of subspace size. If it is still falling steeply at the\n"
"largest $d$, the classical solver's dimension cap is the binding constraint and `MAX_DIMENSION` is the\n"
"parameter to increase. If it has flattened, adding more of the retained determinants offers little improvement;\n"
"further progress may require sampling additional configurations. The\n"
"Hamiltonian is built once at full size and every rung is a principal block of it, so the whole\n"
"sweep costs one matrix build rather than one per rung.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Adakah ia sudah menumpu?** Susun semula penentu yang dikekalkan mengikut beratnya dalam vektor eigen yang menumpu\n"
"dan subruang menjadi *bersarang*, jadi pepenjuruan blok $d \\times d$ yang utama untuk satu tangga nilai $d$\n"
"menjejak penurunan sempadan merentasi dua dekad saiz subruang. Jika ia masih menurun dengan curam pada\n"
"$d$ terbesar, had dimensi pemecah klasik ialah kekangan yang mengikat dan `MAX_DIMENSION` ialah\n"
"parameter yang perlu dinaikkan. Jika ia sudah mendatar, menambah lebih banyak penentu yang dikekalkan hanya memberi sedikit peningkatan;\n"
"kemajuan selanjutnya mungkin memerlukan persampelan konfigurasi tambahan. Hamiltonian\n"
"dibina sekali pada saiz penuh dan setiap anak tangga ialah blok utama daripadanya, jadi seluruh\n"
"sapuan hanya memerlukan satu pembinaan matriks, bukan satu setiap anak tangga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**How does quantum sampling compare with classical selection?** Compare with a subspace of the\n"
"same size chosen by the classical selection procedure: take the pool ranked by perturbation theory in score\n"
"order, grow the product subspace to the same dimension, and diagonalize that instead. Both curves are\n"
"rigorous upper bounds on the same Hamiltonian, so whichever sits lower at equal dimension picked the\n"
"better determinants. This comparison decides whether hardware sampling improves the energy estimate\n"
"relative to this classical baseline.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Bagaimana persampelan kuantum berbanding pemilihan klasik?** Bandingkan dengan subruang yang\n"
"sama saiz yang dipilih melalui prosedur pemilihan klasik: ambil kolam yang disusun mengikut teori usikan dalam tertib\n"
"skor, besarkan subruang hasil darab kepada dimensi yang sama, dan pepenjuruankan yang itu sebaliknya. Kedua-dua lengkung ialah\n"
"sempadan atas yang tegar bagi Hamiltonian yang sama, jadi mana yang lebih rendah pada dimensi yang sama telah memilih\n"
"penentu yang lebih baik. Perbandingan ini menentukan sama ada persampelan perkakasan memperbaik anggaran tenaga\n"
"berbanding garis asas klasik ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This subspace is not selected for excited states. Configuration recovery steers the subspace\n"
"using ground-state occupancies, so the higher eigenvalues are much further from converged than the\n"
"lowest one, and the first excitation energy comes out well above the measured $2^+$. Reaching excited\n"
"states properly needs a subspace selected for them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Subruang ini tidak dipilih untuk keadaan teruja. Pemulihan konfigurasi mengemudi subruang\n"
"menggunakan pendudukan keadaan asas, jadi nilai eigen yang lebih tinggi jauh lebih jauh daripada menumpu berbanding yang\n"
"terendah, dan tenaga pengujaan pertama keluar jauh melebihi $2^+$ yang diukur. Untuk mencapai keadaan\n"
"teruja dengan betul, subruang yang dipilih khusus untuknya diperlukan.\n"

