# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extensions to consider {#extensions-to-consider}"
msgstr "Sambungan untuk dipertimbangkan {#extensions-to-consider}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Replace the dense solver.** `MAX_DIMENSION` is the ceiling on everything at the $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$\n"
"scale, and `np.linalg.eigh` on a dense matrix is why. Building the same projected\n"
"Hamiltonian as a sparse matrix and using an iterative eigensolver such as\n"
"`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh`, or a Davidson or selected-CI solver designed for nuclear two-body\n"
"interactions, could support larger subspaces. The practical limit depends on matrix sparsity,\n"
"available memory, and solver convergence, and this tutorial does not benchmark that extension. The SQD addon's `qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_sci` is not a drop-in substitute: it wraps an\n"
"electronic-structure solver and expects one- and two-body integrals in that form, so the shared\n"
"proton $\\times$ neutron product structure is not sufficient on its own. Using it would mean mapping\n"
"the shell-model interaction of Equation (1) into those integrals and validating the result against the\n"
"exact energies this notebook already computes.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Gantikan pemecah padat.** `MAX_DIMENSION` ialah siling bagi segalanya pada skala $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$,\n"
"dan `np.linalg.eigh` pada matriks padat ialah puncanya. Membina Hamiltonian terunjur yang sama\n"
"sebagai matriks jarang dan menggunakan pemecah eigen lelaran seperti\n"
"`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh`, atau pemecah Davidson atau selected-CI yang direka untuk interaksi dua-jasad\n"
"nuklear, boleh menyokong subruang yang lebih besar. Had praktikal bergantung pada kejarangan matriks,\n"
"memori yang ada, dan penumpuan pemecah, dan tutorial ini tidak membuat penanda aras sambungan itu. `qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_sci` milik addon SQD bukan pengganti terus: ia membungkus pemecah\n"
"struktur elektronik dan menjangka kamiran satu dan dua jasad dalam bentuk itu, jadi struktur hasil darab\n"
"proton $\\times$ neutron yang dikongsi tidak mencukupi dengan sendirinya. Menggunakannya bermakna memetakan\n"
"interaksi model petala Persamaan (1) kepada kamiran tersebut dan mengesahkan hasilnya berbanding\n"
"tenaga tepat yang sudah dikira oleh notebook ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Add batching and subsampling.** The published pooled SQD workflow diagonalizes several independent\n"
"subsamples per iteration and keeps the best. This tutorial uses one batch per iteration, which is\n"
"harmless for the variational bound but does not provide the variance information that indicates whether more shots\n"
"would help.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tambah batching dan subpersampelan.** Aliran kerja SQD terkumpul yang diterbitkan mempepenjuruankan beberapa subsampel\n"
"bebas bagi setiap lelaran dan mengekalkan yang terbaik. Tutorial ini menggunakan satu batch bagi setiap lelaran, yang\n"
"tidak menjejaskan sempadan variasi tetapi tidak memberikan maklumat varians yang menunjukkan sama ada lebih banyak shot\n"
"akan membantu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Excited states and other sectors.** The higher eigenvalues of each subspace Hamiltonian are upper\n"
"bounds on excited states in the same symmetry sector, and running at $M_J \\neq 0$ reaches other\n"
"sectors. The $2^+$ check in Step 1 is already half of this calculation.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Keadaan teruja dan sektor lain.** Nilai eigen yang lebih tinggi bagi setiap Hamiltonian subruang ialah sempadan\n"
"atas bagi keadaan teruja dalam sektor simetri yang sama, dan menjalankan pada $M_J \\neq 0$ mencapai sektor\n"
"lain. Semakan $2^+$ dalam Langkah 1 sudah separuh daripada pengiraan ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A cross-shell model space.** Parity is automatically satisfied inside a single major shell, which\n"
"is why it does no work here. An $sd$-$pf$ space mixes $\\ell$ parities, making parity a genuine\n"
"fourth constraint, one that neither SQD's Hamming-weight repair nor the product\n"
"construction would catch on its own.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ruang model silang-petala.** Pariti dipenuhi secara automatik dalam satu petala utama, itulah\n"
"sebabnya ia tidak berfungsi di sini. Ruang $sd$-$pf$ mencampurkan pariti $\\ell$, menjadikan pariti satu\n"
"kekangan keempat yang sebenar, yang tidak akan ditangkap sendiri oleh pembaikan Hamming-weight SQD mahupun\n"
"pembinaan hasil darab.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Odd-mass nuclei.** `reference_determinant` requires an even valence count in each species,\n"
"because a time-reversed paired filling is what forces $M_J = 0$. An odd nucleus needs a\n"
"half-integer $M_J$ target and an unpaired reference.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Nukleus jisim ganjil.** `reference_determinant` memerlukan bilangan valens genap bagi setiap spesies,\n"
"kerana pengisian berpasangan songsang masa itulah yang memaksa $M_J = 0$. Nukleus ganjil memerlukan\n"
"sasaran $M_J$ separuh integer dan rujukan yang tidak berpasangan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Appendix {#appendix}"
msgstr "Lampiran {#appendix}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This section explains the reasoning behind the helpers introduced in the [Setup](#setup) section.\n"
msgstr "Bahagian ini menerangkan sebab di sebalik pembantu yang diperkenalkan dalam bahagian [Persediaan](#setup).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why the mass-dependence rescaling is not optional {#why-the-mass-dependence-rescaling-is-not-optional}"
msgstr "Mengapa penskalaan semula kebergantungan jisim tidak boleh diabaikan {#why-the-mass-dependence-rescaling-is-not-optional}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Empirical shell-model interactions are fitted at one mass and applied across a chain of isotopes, with\n"
"the two-body matrix elements scaled as $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{p}$. Both interaction files carry\n"
"$p = -0.3$, with $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ for the USD family and $42$ for GXPF1. On the two-body header\n"
"line of a `.snt` file, those two numbers sit where an oscillator frequency and a core energy would\n"
"plausibly go, which makes them easy to misread; reading the exponent as a constant core energy adds a\n"
"spurious offset to every diagonal element *and* drops the rescaling, changing the correlation energy by\n"
"a few percent. The symmetry check in Step 1 does not by itself verify the energy scale. Comparing\n"
"the $2^+$ excitation energy, measured in MeV, with experiment provides an additional check on the\n"
"mass-dependent rescaling. An excitation energy is a difference between levels, so it does not\n"
"detect a constant offset applied to all energies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Interaksi model petala empirik disuaikan pada satu jisim dan diterapkan merentasi rantaian isotop, dengan\n"
"elemen matriks dua-jasad diskalakan sebagai $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{p}$. Kedua-dua fail interaksi membawa\n"
"$p = -0.3$, dengan $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ untuk keluarga USD dan $42$ untuk GXPF1. Pada baris pengepala\n"
"dua-jasad dalam fail `.snt`, kedua-dua nombor itu terletak di tempat frekuensi pengayun dan tenaga teras\n"
"lazimnya berada, menjadikannya mudah disalah baca; membaca eksponen sebagai tenaga teras malar menambah\n"
"ofset palsu pada setiap unsur pepenjuru *dan* menggugurkan penskalaan semula, mengubah tenaga korelasi sebanyak\n"
"beberapa peratus. Semakan simetri dalam Langkah 1 tidak mengesahkan skala tenaga dengan sendirinya. Membandingkan\n"
"tenaga pengujaan $2^+$, diukur dalam MeV, dengan eksperimen memberikan semakan tambahan terhadap penskalaan semula\n"
"bergantung jisim. Tenaga pengujaan ialah perbezaan antara aras, jadi ia tidak\n"
"mengesan ofset malar yang dikenakan pada semua tenaga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why the reference is found by search rather than by filling {#why-the-reference-is-found-by-search-rather-than-by-filling}"
msgstr "Mengapa rujukan dicari melalui carian dan bukan melalui pengisian {#why-the-reference-is-found-by-search-rather-than-by-filling}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The obvious reference is the determinant that fills the lowest single-particle energies. It is not the\n"
"lowest-energy determinant, because the diagonal of Equation (1) includes the two-body term\n"
"$\\sum_{i<j} \\langle ij \\| ij \\rangle$, and the pairing interaction strongly prefers occupying\n"
"time-reversed $(+m_j, -m_j)$ partners in the *largest* available $|m_j|$. In the $sd$ shell that is the\n"
"difference between the $m_j = \\pm 1/2$ pair and the $m_j = \\pm 5/2$ pair of $0d_{5/2}$, and it is worth\n"
"about 1 MeV; in the $pf$ shell, it is worth closer to 2. Because the reference energy defines the zero of the\n"
"\"correlation energy recovered\" metric, a poor choice inflates that metric and gives a less accurate\n"
"starting point.\n"
msgstr ""
"Rujukan yang jelas ialah penentu yang mengisi tenaga zarah tunggal terendah. Ia bukan\n"
"penentu bertenaga terendah, kerana pepenjuru Persamaan (1) merangkumi sebutan dua-jasad\n"
"$\\sum_{i<j} \\langle ij \\| ij \\rangle$, dan interaksi pasangan sangat cenderung menduduki\n"
"pasangan songsang masa $(+m_j, -m_j)$ pada $|m_j|$ *terbesar* yang ada. Dalam petala $sd$ itulah\n"
"perbezaan antara pasangan $m_j = \\pm 1/2$ dan pasangan $m_j = \\pm 5/2$ bagi $0d_{5/2}$, dan nilainya\n"
"kira-kira 1 MeV; dalam petala $pf$, nilainya hampir 2. Oleh sebab tenaga rujukan menentukan sifar bagi metrik\n"
"\"tenaga korelasi yang dipulihkan\", pilihan yang buruk membesarkan metrik itu dan memberikan titik\n"
"permulaan yang kurang tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Restricting to paired fillings makes exhaustive search inexpensive, with $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ candidates per\n"
"species (a few thousand at most), and ensures $M_J = 0$. In every case in this\n"
"tutorial that can be checked against a full enumeration, the search returns the global lowest-diagonal\n"
"determinant, which is also the single largest component of the exact ground state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menghadkan kepada pengisian berpasangan menjadikan carian menyeluruh murah, dengan $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ calon bagi setiap\n"
"spesies (paling banyak beberapa ribu), dan memastikan $M_J = 0$. Dalam setiap kes dalam\n"
"tutorial ini yang boleh disemak dengan penghitungan penuh, carian itu memulangkan penentu pepenjuru\n"
"terendah global, yang juga merupakan komponen tunggal terbesar bagi keadaan asas tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why the first-order amplitude, not the exact two-level angle {#why-the-first-order-amplitude-not-the-exact-two-level-angle}"
msgstr "Mengapa amplitud tertib pertama, bukan sudut dua aras yang tepat {#why-the-first-order-amplitude-not-the-exact-two-level-angle}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Diagonalizing the $2 \\times 2$ Hamiltonian in the space\n"
"$\\{|\\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}}\\rangle, |\\alpha\\rangle\\}$ gives the mixing angle\n"
"$\\theta_{\\mathrm{exact}} = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\arctan(2V/\\Delta)$; it might be tempting to call that the correct\n"
"choice for an *isolated* pair of levels. In this ansatz, several dozen excitation blocks act\n"
"in sequence on the same reference, so optimizing each block separately does not necessarily\n"
"optimize the composite circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mempepenjuruankan Hamiltonian $2 \\times 2$ dalam ruang\n"
"$\\{|\\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}}\\rangle, |\\alpha\\rangle\\}$ memberikan sudut campuran\n"
"$\\theta_{\\mathrm{exact}} = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\arctan(2V/\\Delta)$; mungkin menggoda untuk menyebutnya pilihan\n"
"yang betul bagi sepasang aras yang *terpencil*. Dalam ansatz ini, beberapa dozen blok pengujaan bertindak\n"
"secara berurutan pada rujukan yang sama, jadi mengoptimumkan setiap blok secara berasingan tidak semestinya\n"
"mengoptimumkan circuit gubahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The circuit’s role determines the choice of angle. Since\n"
"$|\\tfrac{1}{2}\\arctan(2x)| \\le |x|$ for every real $x$, the exact angle is always *smaller* in\n"
"magnitude than the first-order amplitude $t = V/\\Delta$, and therefore always leaves *more* amplitude\n"
"on the reference determinant. A circuit that keeps more amplitude on the reference returns the\n"
"reference more often and distinct excited determinants less often. For pooled SQD, the useful output of a shot\n"
"is a determinant the classical step has not seen yet, which motivates using the larger angle in this tutorial. Neither angle needs to be accurate, because the classical diagonalization discards the circuit's\n"
"amplitudes entirely and re-derives its own.\n"
msgstr ""
"Peranan circuit menentukan pilihan sudut. Oleh sebab\n"
"$|\\tfrac{1}{2}\\arctan(2x)| \\le |x|$ untuk setiap $x$ nyata, sudut tepat sentiasa *lebih kecil* dari segi\n"
"besaran daripada amplitud tertib pertama $t = V/\\Delta$, dan oleh itu sentiasa meninggalkan *lebih banyak* amplitud\n"
"pada penentu rujukan. Circuit yang mengekalkan lebih banyak amplitud pada rujukan memulangkan\n"
"rujukan lebih kerap dan penentu teruja yang berbeza lebih jarang. Bagi SQD terkumpul, output berguna bagi sesuatu shot\n"
"ialah penentu yang belum dilihat oleh langkah klasik, yang mendorong penggunaan sudut yang lebih besar dalam tutorial ini. Kedua-dua sudut tidak perlu tepat, kerana pepenjuruan klasik membuang amplitud\n"
"circuit sepenuhnya dan menerbitkan amplitudnya sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why pooled SQD can use qubit excitations {#why-pooled-sqd-can-use-qubit-excitations}"
msgstr "Mengapa SQD terkumpul boleh menggunakan pengujaan qubit {#why-pooled-sqd-can-use-qubit-excitations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fermionic excitation $T = a_{v_1}^\\dagger a_{v_2}^\\dagger a_{h_2} a_{h_1}$ maps under\n"
"Jordan-Wigner to eight Pauli strings, each carrying $Z$ operators on every qubit between the outermost\n"
"indices. Those strings encode the fermionic sign, and their cost grows with the span, which for a\n"
"proton-neutron excitation is the whole register.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengujaan fermion $T = a_{v_1}^\\dagger a_{v_2}^\\dagger a_{h_2} a_{h_1}$ dipetakan di bawah\n"
"Jordan-Wigner kepada lapan rentetan Pauli, masing-masing membawa operator $Z$ pada setiap qubit antara indeks\n"
"terluar. Rentetan itu mengekod tanda fermion, dan kosnya bertambah dengan rentang, yang bagi\n"
"pengujaan proton-neutron ialah keseluruhan daftar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deleting them gives the qubit-excitation operator of Yordanov et al. [\\[5\\]](#references). It is a\n"
"different operator: the state it prepares differs from the fermionic one in the *signs* of\n"
"its amplitudes, and the two sampling distributions can differ substantially. What it does not change\n"
"is which determinants have nonzero amplitude, because each block still rotates within the same\n"
"two-dimensional space $\\{|d\\rangle, |d'\\rangle\\}$ for every determinant $d$ it acts on, and it still\n"
"conserves both nucleon numbers, $M_J$, and parity exactly. The reachable set of determinants is\n"
"therefore identical, and the reachable set is the only thing pooled SQD uses; the classical\n"
"diagonalization assigns its own amplitudes regardless. Step 2 verifies the identical-support claim on\n"
"a real operator from the pool and measures what the substitution saves.\n"
msgstr ""
"Memadamkannya menghasilkan operator pengujaan qubit Yordanov et al. [\\[5\\]](#references). Ia ialah operator\n"
"yang berbeza: keadaan yang disediakannya berbeza daripada keadaan fermion dari segi *tanda*\n"
"amplitudnya, dan kedua-dua taburan persampelan boleh berbeza dengan ketara. Yang tidak diubahnya\n"
"ialah penentu mana yang mempunyai amplitud bukan sifar, kerana setiap blok masih memutar dalam ruang\n"
"dwidimensi yang sama $\\{|d\\rangle, |d'\\rangle\\}$ bagi setiap penentu $d$ yang dikenakannya, dan ia masih\n"
"memelihara kedua-dua bilangan nukleon, $M_J$, dan pariti dengan tepat. Set penentu yang boleh dicapai\n"
"oleh itu adalah sama, dan set yang boleh dicapai itulah satu-satunya yang digunakan oleh SQD terkumpul; pepenjuruan\n"
"klasik menetapkan amplitudnya sendiri tanpa mengira. Langkah 2 mengesahkan dakwaan sokongan yang sama pada\n"
"operator sebenar daripada kolam dan mengukur apa yang dijimatkan oleh penggantian itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The limitation is that the sampling *weights* differ, so the two constructions will not discover\n"
"determinants in the same order at finite shot count. Since the ranking that decides which excitations\n"
"enter the circuits is classical and unchanged, and the classical step re-weights everything anyway,\n"
"the difference in sampling weights is a tradeoff for reduced circuit depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Batasannya ialah *berat* persampelan berbeza, jadi kedua-dua pembinaan tidak akan menemui\n"
"penentu dalam tertib yang sama pada bilangan shot terhingga. Oleh sebab kedudukan yang menentukan pengujaan mana\n"
"memasuki circuit adalah klasik dan tidak berubah, dan langkah klasik menimbang semula segalanya,\n"
"perbezaan berat persampelan ialah pertukaran demi kedalaman circuit yang dikurangkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why $M_J$ belongs to the product stage {#why-m-j-belongs-to-the-product-stage}"
msgstr "Mengapa $M_J$ tergolong dalam peringkat hasil darab {#why-m-j-belongs-to-the-product-stage}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Post-selection and configuration recovery both act on Hamming weights: the number of protons in one\n"
"half of the register, and the number of neutrons in the other. $M_J = M_p + M_n$ is not of that form. It is a property of a proton configuration *paired with* a neutron configuration. A shot whose proton\n"
"half and neutron half each carry the right nucleon number contains two usable half-configurations even\n"
"when their $M_J$ values do not cancel, because the proton half at $M_p = +1$ is perfectly good once it\n"
"is paired with a neutron half at $M_n = -1$. Filtering whole shots on total $M_J$ throws both halves\n"
"away, and imposing $M_J$ on the recombined products keeps them. The same argument explains why\n"
"`recover_configurations` needs no notion of $M_J$ to be useful in this case.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pasca-pemilihan dan pemulihan konfigurasi kedua-duanya bertindak pada Hamming weight: bilangan proton dalam satu\n"
"setengah daftar, dan bilangan neutron dalam setengah lagi. $M_J = M_p + M_n$ bukan dalam bentuk itu. Ia ialah sifat konfigurasi proton yang *dipasangkan dengan* konfigurasi neutron. Shot yang setengah proton\n"
"dan setengah neutronnya masing-masing membawa bilangan nukleon yang betul mengandungi dua separuh konfigurasi yang boleh digunakan walaupun\n"
"nilai $M_J$ mereka tidak membatalkan, kerana separuh proton pada $M_p = +1$ adalah sangat baik sebaik sahaja\n"
"ia dipasangkan dengan separuh neutron pada $M_n = -1$. Menapis keseluruhan shot pada $M_J$ jumlah membuang kedua-dua\n"
"setengah, dan mengenakan $M_J$ pada hasil darab yang digabungkan semula mengekalkannya. Hujah yang sama menerangkan sebab\n"
"`recover_configurations` tidak memerlukan tanggapan $M_J$ untuk berguna dalam kes ini.\n"

